00:52.533 --> 00:56.061
Okay, so with that, our first discussion item under

00:56.561 --> 00:59.267
this work session is our sports and recreation planning.

01:03.396 --> 01:06.696
And Jason, is it Jason? Jason, are you presenting this or who's—

01:07.196 --> 01:10.366
Yes, sir. Okay, Jason Hall, would you come up and share your

01:10.962 --> 01:12.513
expertise and experience with us?

01:17.742 --> 01:21.044
Legacy of coordinating sports

01:21.093 --> 01:25.535
and recreation programming in Eagle Mountain.

01:25.730 --> 01:30.885
All right,

01:33.887 --> 01:36.872
all right. Well,

01:36.888 --> 01:40.460
thanks for having me over, guys. I was just asked to come and talk about

01:41.602 --> 01:45.272
kind of our programs and what we have going on and stuff along

01:45.384 --> 01:47.705
those lines. So we'll just get started.

01:50.398 --> 01:53.729
So this is just a quick look at programs

01:54.229 --> 01:57.916
that we currently run through the city. These are programs our staff handles

01:58.012 --> 02:01.612
from start to finish. You can see the youth programs

02:02.270 --> 02:06.295
and adult programs that we run currently with

02:06.795 --> 02:10.860
the staff that we have. And these are

02:11.360 --> 02:15.162
our programs by season. So this shows our programs spread

02:15.194 --> 02:18.418
throughout the year. We pretty much have something going

02:18.499 --> 02:22.307
on during every season. And we have

02:22.807 --> 02:26.440
a lot of programs that do overlap and so forth on that end.

02:29.644 --> 02:33.396
And these are programs that either we support

02:33.896 --> 02:37.265
through partnerships or outsourcing. Field rentals.

02:38.340 --> 02:41.600
Even though we don't run the programs, our staff is still involved in this

02:41.777 --> 02:45.132
with scheduling fields and communications

02:45.164 --> 02:48.183
and different things along those lines.

02:49.018 --> 02:51.892
We do like baseball, stuff like that.

02:52.775 --> 02:56.886
Baseball, girls fastpitch softball, we prep all the

02:57.386 --> 03:00.129
fields and stuff for them. So we make sure that those are prepped and ready

03:00.629 --> 03:03.711
to go for them. That's pretty much what we do. we spend. Oh,

03:04.530 --> 03:07.646
okay. Can I ask you a question since I'm seeing it?

03:07.710 --> 03:11.340
What's Snapology? So Snapology, it's a STEM class

03:11.840 --> 03:15.436
is what it is. Okay. So that one we, that one we

03:15.516 --> 03:19.291
partnership with Snapology. I think they're called Snapology of Lehi.

03:19.435 --> 03:23.306
They're, they're all over the county and Salt Lake County as well. But yeah,

03:23.387 --> 03:26.744
it's kind of cool. It's Legos and stuff. They build them and

03:26.760 --> 03:29.909
they actually They get to— they build robots out of them and stuff, get to

03:29.957 --> 03:33.605
drive them. It's pretty good. We have a— during the summer,

03:33.733 --> 03:37.028
we run a camp. We run like 3 or 4 camps with

03:37.528 --> 03:40.884
them, so they're a week long. We actually hold them here in the

03:41.384 --> 03:45.544
council chamber. So, and right now we have one. We have— we

03:46.044 --> 03:49.175
had— we just started fall one with them, but it's just

03:49.675 --> 03:52.807
one night a week. It's every Thursday that we do that with them. Very cool.

03:53.160 --> 03:54.663
It's a pretty good turnout for those.

03:58.116 --> 04:01.467
And so these are some of the programs, activities that we'd

04:01.483 --> 04:05.657
like to add. Obviously, this depends completely

04:05.834 --> 04:09.633
on space and

04:09.714 --> 04:13.676
staff, really. With the staff we have right now, we're pretty much to

04:14.176 --> 04:17.807
max on what we're able to accomplish with the hours that we have and

04:17.888 --> 04:21.343
so forth. But we do have a couple positions that are

04:21.843 --> 04:26.192
open. They're just part-time, but they will help alleviate some of the staff,

04:26.257 --> 04:29.259
and we'll be able to add a few more programs and stuff.

04:30.191 --> 04:34.060
Can I ask a question on those other recreation activities? So would

04:35.313 --> 04:38.829
the city ever get involved in like astronomy type things? I know we have

04:38.861 --> 04:42.105
a lot of that money committed to do that. Yeah, we've adopted stuff like that.

04:42.153 --> 04:44.385
And I know UVU's involved with that too, but I didn't know if the city—

04:44.885 --> 04:48.735
Yeah, we want— there's like, you know, science and STEM

04:49.235 --> 04:52.089
programs, chess club, and different stuff like that that we would love to do,

04:52.587 --> 04:55.893
different classes and stuff along those lines that we would love to do.

04:56.021 --> 04:59.311
So again, that depends. We obviously— you guys know

04:59.811 --> 05:01.895
we don't have rec center, we don't have, we don't have a building period that

05:02.395 --> 05:05.635
we can actually hold something in. So it's either we rent from the schools,

05:06.389 --> 05:09.534
and that's hard because they're busy, especially right now, right? And so trying

05:10.034 --> 05:12.910
to rent that, and then Once you figure in those fees, you've got to add

05:13.410 --> 05:16.214
those in. And so it gets a little pricey when it comes to that end.

05:19.202 --> 05:22.431
So these are our youth programs. This shows kind of

05:22.931 --> 05:25.757
the growth that we've had for junior jazz, soccer, baseball,

05:27.236 --> 05:29.857
all those— all the other programs that we've had.

05:30.598 --> 05:35.107
Obviously basketball and soccer. And now soccer— soccer

05:35.607 --> 05:37.812
we used to run, then we outsourced it, and we just brought it back.

05:38.427 --> 05:42.391
for this fall season. So, and we had about 800,

05:42.439 --> 05:45.103
a little over 800 kids sign up this year for fall soccer.

05:46.371 --> 05:50.351
So it's been, it's been busy. It's been real busy for us. So that's

05:50.464 --> 05:53.497
on top of trying to keep fields prepped and, and everything else.

05:53.689 --> 05:56.867
So we did have track and field, cross country,

05:56.899 --> 05:59.596
and youth pickleball. Those have been good numbers.

06:00.109 --> 06:03.463
We added those a couple years ago, or about, yeah, 2024, I think.

06:03.544 --> 06:07.793
2024. And they've slowly been increasing on

06:08.084 --> 06:09.571
our numbers on those as well.

06:13.030 --> 06:16.296
Adult programs. Adult programs

06:16.328 --> 06:20.289
have grown too as well. As you can see those— and they

06:20.789 --> 06:24.788
fluctuate just depending on which program. Like usually our co-ed softball

06:24.886 --> 06:28.010
has always been the highest number of teams to sign up. But this year was

06:28.123 --> 06:31.810
actually a lot lower and our men's league was— had

06:31.826 --> 06:35.356
a lot more teams sign up than our co-ed did, which is— it's weird,

06:35.372 --> 06:37.629
but it is this, right? It's always up and down.

06:39.312 --> 06:42.757
And this is just obviously a chart

06:43.257 --> 06:47.701
that gives a look of, you know, back from 2008 up to this

06:48.201 --> 06:51.120
year, kind of where our numbers are growing just for a couple of our bigger

06:51.136 --> 06:54.381
programs. So as you can tell, we've grown quite

06:54.446 --> 06:55.253
a lot. So.

06:57.408 --> 07:02.459
So this is kind of where we're stuck

07:02.959 --> 07:06.690
with our restraints, limited gym space. So that's, it seems funny

07:07.190 --> 07:08.865
'cause you say that, 'cause like we rent all the schools and you say,

07:08.881 --> 07:12.168
well, we've added elementary schools and stuff like that, but we've been behind,

07:12.345 --> 07:16.653
right, on gym spaces as it is. So, and you keep adding more

07:16.782 --> 07:21.135
kids and it takes away the gym space, plus you have other programs

07:21.232 --> 07:24.818
that— You know, your competitive programs and stuff

07:25.318 --> 07:29.378
that also rent gym space from them. So it does take away some

07:29.394 --> 07:33.841
of our gym space use on that. And so

07:34.114 --> 07:37.647
we're— but we're still getting there. We had to— when we first started

07:38.147 --> 07:41.356
programs for like Junior Jazz, we used to be able to give

07:41.856 --> 07:45.547
the younger kids practice times. We had to shift that because we ran

07:45.675 --> 07:49.413
out. We're getting slower. We're being getting less gym

07:49.445 --> 07:53.036
time. So the younger kids, we had to move their practices to before

07:53.536 --> 07:56.418
the games. And so that's— it's worked out pretty good. I mean, that's what a

07:56.918 --> 08:00.330
lot of cities do anyways. So it's just a matter of adapting and

08:00.426 --> 08:03.936
getting what we can do. Jason, in that— in the

08:04.436 --> 08:07.671
context of school gyms, as the indoor

08:07.960 --> 08:11.439
sports season approaches, do you reach out

08:11.631 --> 08:15.655
to the Alpine School District and say, hey, What's available and

08:16.155 --> 08:19.534
then you reserve times based on what's available, or do you tell them what you'd

08:19.566 --> 08:22.821
like? So we basically— we don't tell them, we ask them.

08:23.109 --> 08:26.700
We ask them with a paycheck? Yes. With a check in mind,

08:26.716 --> 08:29.057
right? Paycheck, upfront money. No.

08:29.778 --> 08:32.487
So what we do is we submit. You have to go in and submit for

08:32.987 --> 08:35.790
what you need. Okay. And then they'll look at it and they'll either— they'll call

08:36.290 --> 08:38.820
me and say, okay, we have this going on or this going on, so we

08:39.320 --> 08:42.604
can't do this night or this night or whatever, you know, we have different activities.

08:42.668 --> 08:46.212
So there's, there's a lot of back and forth a little bit. So— Okay.

08:46.597 --> 08:49.980
But usually I have an idea of what they have going on from

08:50.480 --> 08:53.011
the year before because we keep notes and all that stuff. So I'm able to

08:53.511 --> 08:57.068
just plug those in and get them over. And so far— and

08:57.084 --> 08:59.441
I submitted these usually, you know,

08:59.890 --> 09:03.996
summertime they're usually off. It's hit and miss. And we try

09:04.496 --> 09:08.006
to get it done before July, but We submit them and I've still

09:08.506 --> 09:11.215
got 3 or 4 schools that haven't even reached out to me on that,

09:11.296 --> 09:14.714
which is worrisome. Are you dealing with each school

09:14.827 --> 09:18.037
separately versus— Yes, each school is separate. Oh, okay.

09:18.261 --> 09:22.498
Yep, yep, each one of them has their own person

09:22.514 --> 09:25.853
who's over their rentals. Okay. And they're the ones that tell us

09:25.885 --> 09:29.640
yes or no, or this is what we have going on. Are charter schools

09:29.817 --> 09:33.733
part of that or is it just Alpine School District? Ranches Academy,

09:33.830 --> 09:36.880
we tried to rent them before and they told us no. They just—

09:37.380 --> 09:41.231
no. We haven't— I think when John Hancock

09:41.731 --> 09:44.683
first opened, we reached out to them and they told us no. Okay. But I

09:45.183 --> 09:48.794
have heard since they said, yeah, we can probably rent to you. So just a

09:49.294 --> 09:52.294
matter of reaching out. Just depends. Okay. Yeah. Yeah. Thanks. So,

09:52.454 --> 09:55.890
and the high school's hard because they have so many clubs, programs,

09:55.922 --> 09:59.635
and different stuff that theirs is hard because They do

09:59.700 --> 10:03.538
give us some times, but it's all over the place every

10:03.570 --> 10:07.408
week. So it's hard to run a program when you're not consistent on days.

10:11.141 --> 10:14.287
So right now, this is kind of what we have for staffing. We've got 3

10:14.787 --> 10:17.996
full-time employees. Seasonal staff

10:18.496 --> 10:21.718
is actually a little bit higher than that now, just with our site

10:22.218 --> 10:24.226
supervisors, soccer referees.

10:25.779 --> 10:29.697
Junior Jazz referees and so forth. And like I said, we do have 2

10:29.729 --> 10:33.711
positions, part-time positions open for recreation coordinators and

10:33.808 --> 10:37.886
2 for athletic maintenance employees,

10:38.143 --> 10:42.109
which will help a lot because right now we

10:42.735 --> 10:46.829
prep fields in the morning and then a lot of— we

10:47.329 --> 10:49.447
prep in the morning and then we'll go home for a few hours and come

10:49.479 --> 10:53.493
back at night. So getting these extra staff

10:53.557 --> 10:56.592
will definitely help us out on that end.

10:58.069 --> 11:01.280
Are your field prep staff different than the parks?

11:01.666 --> 11:04.508
Well, I know the park has been maintained by contract,

11:04.556 --> 11:07.944
right? So the mowing and irrigation repair,

11:07.976 --> 11:10.979
that's all being done separately. That's not your staff that's dealing with that.

11:11.075 --> 11:14.286
It was ours for a while, but we just couldn't keep up,

11:14.447 --> 11:18.620
and the parks department took over the soccer fields and on

11:19.120 --> 11:22.560
the irrigation side. They took over the soccer fields and all that stuff and they've

11:23.060 --> 11:26.660
done an amazing job. So they've definitely brought it up.

11:27.160 --> 11:31.180
They've had to pull resources from other places to help, especially with soccer coming

11:31.680 --> 11:34.770
in because there's a lot of wear and tear on that end.

11:35.200 --> 11:38.640
So— Got a question for you, just going backwards a little bit. You're good.

11:39.140 --> 11:42.880
But I know there's a lot of constraint with youth sports and

11:43.380 --> 11:46.791
field space and all this stuff. Are there similar constraints with adult

11:47.082 --> 11:50.718
sports like softball or pickleball or anything of

11:51.218 --> 11:54.276
those nature? Yeah, so that's why for adult

11:54.292 --> 11:57.674
softball, we only run

11:58.174 --> 12:02.253
in the fall because we can't run anything in the spring because youth baseball

12:02.528 --> 12:06.312
is there Monday through Saturday. We don't have any— we don't

12:06.812 --> 12:10.945
have any open time to run anything. And we've been asked a lot to To

12:11.445 --> 12:14.624
do spring adult softball, but right now

12:15.124 --> 12:17.982
it's just not possible. Yeah, and if they had more fields and space, then you'd

12:18.062 --> 12:21.195
probably need more staff to help maintain all that too at the same time.

12:21.340 --> 12:24.826
Yeah, yeah, yeah, we definitely need more fields, but like you

12:24.874 --> 12:29.212
said, we do need more staff for that. I think if

12:29.712 --> 12:33.405
that's a possibility, if you're looking to build more, if we build another

12:33.469 --> 12:36.602
quadplex, if it's there at Cory-Ride

12:37.102 --> 12:40.590
would be ideal, 'Cause that would be best for not having to travel or

12:41.090 --> 12:44.150
whatever. We can have one person that's just there and then just moves over to

12:44.650 --> 12:48.290
another quadplex and stuff instead of having to pack up equipment. I don't

12:48.790 --> 12:51.730
know if you know, but on the city side of it, is there— outside of

12:52.230 --> 12:55.330
just like coaches, I guess, is there any room for like volunteers to help with

12:55.830 --> 12:58.750
some of that stuff? Yeah, there's been some people who volunteered to help. We actually

12:59.250 --> 13:02.830
had a group, a youth baseball group that was actually— they

13:03.330 --> 13:06.430
actually just started doing it. They started working on the rodeo grounds over there.

13:06.872 --> 13:10.069
Those fields because we don't. We didn't have time to get to it. Parks didn't

13:10.569 --> 13:12.897
have time to get to it, so they were actually out there working on it.

13:13.620 --> 13:17.299
They did a good job keeping it up. But those are

13:17.799 --> 13:20.898
things we we have four fields that we use constantly for games,

13:21.412 --> 13:24.529
and then we just have the fields at Nolan and the one at the

13:25.029 --> 13:29.140
rodeo grounds. And the problem with problem with ones at Nolan: you've got

13:29.640 --> 13:33.141
soccer teams that want to practice there, tackle football teams that practice

13:33.641 --> 13:37.651
there. Flag football teams that go and practice there. So it's hard to

13:38.261 --> 13:41.775
play baseball and soccer and everything all at the same time because you got balls

13:41.872 --> 13:45.579
going flying past everyone's head. So, so that makes

13:46.079 --> 13:50.442
it pretty difficult out there. Are you— I'm guessing the city is also renting

13:50.714 --> 13:53.539
field space during the outdoor, whether it's soccer,

13:54.085 --> 13:57.535
baseball, from the school districts, or are you not? Okay, no,

13:57.936 --> 14:01.097
no. And, and we can definitely look at that, but Well, there are

14:01.289 --> 14:04.496
a lot of the club soccer programs, they rent

14:04.996 --> 14:08.506
from the schools. Oh, okay. On that end. So schools exclude that? Yeah.

14:08.666 --> 14:12.018
Gotcha. And we do have— we've gotten quite a high demand

14:12.274 --> 14:16.379
ever since we took back soccer for competitive for the soccer

14:16.879 --> 14:20.597
groups. There's a lot of them that have requested it for field rentals.

14:21.287 --> 14:24.558
So it's a matter of if we can. It's hard.

14:24.863 --> 14:28.006
We've looked at moving some

14:28.506 --> 14:31.525
Some of our fields to different areas within the city. But it's

14:32.025 --> 14:36.518
hard, it's nice to have everything at Corey Ride because when you have a kindergartner

14:37.018 --> 14:40.404
playing and then a second grader and you're here, but if you got one

14:40.597 --> 14:44.691
here and then you got one over at Smith Ranch, that's hard to

14:45.191 --> 14:48.464
get them around. So if we keep it the same area, it's great. Good.

14:48.785 --> 14:52.817
We had, so we did, We purchased

14:53.317 --> 14:56.947
a field painter this year to paint the fields. And the guy that came out

14:58.522 --> 15:02.526
and helped us set it up and everything, he was talking about how good

15:03.026 --> 15:06.213
of a complex it is and if we can add more to it, we can

15:06.229 --> 15:09.629
get a lot of field rentals. But that's really— we can't really.

15:09.742 --> 15:12.318
This is taken up by all our stuff. But yeah.

15:13.042 --> 15:17.067
Good. So this

15:17.534 --> 15:23.302
is just a kind of breakdown of just one of our staff guys

15:23.802 --> 15:26.770
that preps the fields pretty much full-time. I mean, that's a lot of what they

15:27.270 --> 15:30.554
do. He's a rec coordinator, but he spends the majority of his time out there

15:31.054 --> 15:34.348
just prepping fields in the morning. Gets out there at 7:00 and

15:34.848 --> 15:37.628
he's there until 12:30 or so and then goes home and then comes back.

15:38.435 --> 15:41.615
And that's Monday through Friday. Okay. We even— we have

15:42.567 --> 15:47.295
one of our other staff that comes in actually on Friday nights

15:47.795 --> 15:51.112
to prep fields for Saturday morning. Otherwise, we'd have to be out there around 4

15:51.160 --> 15:54.469
o'clock in the morning trying to get them ready before games start on Saturday.

15:54.534 --> 15:58.052
So they come in after all the games are over on Friday nights and go

15:58.552 --> 16:02.518
prep and get them ready. So a lot of hours

16:02.775 --> 16:06.646
just on baseball fields alone. So— oops.

16:07.851 --> 16:11.915
So I— and I don't know, you know, help from Planning

16:11.947 --> 16:16.074
Commission. I think I think that really what— from

16:16.427 --> 16:19.734
our standpoint, if you guys just— anything that's brought up,

16:19.975 --> 16:22.624
buildings, different things, planning and stuff,

16:23.410 --> 16:27.215
just keep us in mind for different stuff

16:27.424 --> 16:31.036
that's out there. You know, if we add different fields or parks

16:31.536 --> 16:34.198
we're looking to add, if we can make them big enough. Obviously parking. Yeah.

16:34.664 --> 16:38.453
Corey Wright, as much parking as there, we're adding on to the west

16:38.953 --> 16:42.370
side, adding parking there. It's still very tight when

16:42.870 --> 16:46.673
you have 4 programs going on Saturday alone. Parking where the dust

16:46.785 --> 16:50.414
plumes kick up in the afternoon? Yes. From the— They're out there

16:50.430 --> 16:54.685
doing— they're doing the parking lot now. Yeah. And still,

16:54.797 --> 16:58.073
we even moved— we moved 4 fields

16:58.249 --> 17:01.637
over to what we call the Field of Dreams,

17:01.702 --> 17:05.587
which is Mid-Valley. Mid-Valley. We moved 4 of them over there.

17:06.326 --> 17:09.702
to try and help, but it still gets— when you've got baseball going and you

17:10.202 --> 17:14.242
got— Yeah. Soccer going, there's a lot of just little kids alone, little kid

17:14.742 --> 17:20.755
fields. We have 10 of those. And I think we have 6 almost

17:21.255 --> 17:23.784
full-size fields out there. So there's a lot of fields and all that's all at

17:23.817 --> 17:26.840
once. And that's— and right now we've rented to

17:26.986 --> 17:30.705
one group, but that's it just because we don't have— that's

17:31.205 --> 17:34.924
the other thing is is they need somewhere to play

17:35.424 --> 17:39.053
too, because a lot of these are kids that live here, right? Yeah. And so

17:39.553 --> 17:42.973
they need somewhere to play too, but the wear and tear on the fields is

17:43.085 --> 17:46.360
hard. So you got to be able to maintain and be able to shift and

17:47.021 --> 17:48.457
tweak the fields as much as you can.

17:50.632 --> 17:55.107
So that was all I had. You guys got— Yeah, so there's a— I

17:55.607 --> 17:59.504
don't know if it's for FTEC, but there's a group looking at different

17:59.681 --> 18:02.923
use, um, recreation, um, projects in our

18:03.423 --> 18:06.005
city. And I think some of them are like redoing some of the parks and

18:06.505 --> 18:09.535
different things. I don't know if that's— I didn't see the details on it,

18:09.568 --> 18:12.922
but I know they're like relooking at a redesign for Nolan Park

18:13.422 --> 18:15.297
as an example and some other stuff. And I don't know if any of that's

18:15.329 --> 18:19.149
going to help with the recreation side of things or just more

18:19.438 --> 18:22.648
other stuff. But— Yeah, I, I don't know much on that end of it,

