51:08.361 --> 51:11.837
Planning Commission, those in the public here tonight,

51:12.561 --> 51:16.050
Corgan Farms is requesting a rezone. There's going to be 2 parts to this.

51:16.244 --> 51:19.230
I will take care of the first part, which is the actual rezone request.

51:19.800 --> 51:23.620
The legal department will then follow up after this item on 7D

51:24.329 --> 51:25.700
as the development agreement.

51:27.640 --> 51:31.222
So the applicant's property, you see here in the red, out here just

51:31.318 --> 51:34.836
southwest of the existing QTS development under

51:35.336 --> 51:38.868
construction. They've come to the city to request that

51:38.884 --> 51:42.323
that parcel be rezoned to the RTI

51:42.404 --> 51:45.630
overlay zone. The underlying zone would be agriculture.

51:46.674 --> 51:50.591
Just a brief of what that means is, in a sense, there's 2 zones

51:51.091 --> 51:54.844
on the property: the agriculture zone, which is the base zone; the

51:55.344 --> 51:58.938
RTI is the overlay. Whatever development then comes in— say

51:59.018 --> 52:02.791
the property is developed or rezoned to the RTI overlay— they

52:03.291 --> 52:06.354
would then follow the code for the RTI overlay, what they could do. If it's

52:06.854 --> 52:10.561
not addressed in the Overlay, and it's not addressed in the subsequent development

52:11.061 --> 52:13.451
agreement. It then defaults to whatever the agriculture zone says.

52:14.543 --> 52:16.984
So, for instance, say there's a setback; it's not listed.

52:17.819 --> 52:20.950
They would follow whatever setback zone would apply,

52:21.288 --> 52:23.536
or setback from the zone that would apply.

52:24.965 --> 52:29.268
And so, what we're looking at—they have approximately

52:29.445 --> 52:33.845
well. First off, the Eagle Mountain Code defines

52:33.941 --> 52:37.886
the purpose of the. RTI as development and operation

52:38.386 --> 52:42.822
of large-scale technological clean industrial and high-tech manufacturing

52:42.838 --> 52:46.347
uses that will increase the tax base and/or provide

52:46.379 --> 52:49.873
jobs for the city's residents. And so the applicant has

52:49.905 --> 52:53.975
requested that the RTI— they own 41

52:54.475 --> 52:58.125
acres. The RTI overlay currently exists on the north,

52:58.462 --> 53:02.019
the east, and the south side of the subject property.

53:02.117 --> 53:06.064
To the west is Utah County jurisdiction governed by their

53:06.564 --> 53:09.645
standards. At this time there is

53:09.694 --> 53:13.478
no development proposal. It's strictly they want to get the zone in place

53:13.978 --> 53:16.955
because that will then be the next step would then be to follow whatever the

53:17.455 --> 53:21.177
standards are for RTI development, whatever it may be, to then pursue a

53:21.242 --> 53:22.908
particular development on the property.

53:25.440 --> 53:28.822
So again, with this there would be a follow-up which again the

53:29.322 --> 53:33.859
legal department will take care of. as far as that, but within the

53:34.599 --> 53:37.708
proposed agreement, it does enumerate some accessory uses,

53:38.287 --> 53:42.391
which are listed here on the screen as well. Again, those are accessory. You'd have

53:42.423 --> 53:46.177
to have primary uses that use the accessory uses. The accessory uses cannot

53:46.226 --> 53:50.053
just come in on their own. And it's

53:50.118 --> 53:53.723
difficult to show on the map, but it does show the zoning map. There's the

53:54.223 --> 53:57.455
arrow pointing to the subject property. Thank you. And then again on

53:57.955 --> 54:00.626
the northeast and the south of that 41-acre square,

54:01.961 --> 54:05.591
the current RTI overlay, if you can see the cross-hatching, does exist

54:05.935 --> 54:07.378
on those parcels there.

54:09.562 --> 54:13.153
