center. It just means we wanted to control how we went forward with the process

55:11.909 --> 55:15.062
because we're— the landowners. Right now, obviously, there's a lot

55:15.562 --> 55:19.920
of negative attention to this type of genre

55:20.420 --> 55:23.688
of— what would you call it— commercial development. And because

55:23.785 --> 55:27.005
I live here, because I work at the high school, and because I plan on

55:27.021 --> 55:30.612
being here for the long term, we didn't want to throw something

55:30.709 --> 55:33.301
up into this property that would affect the residents.

55:33.864 --> 55:37.487
And so I'm up here speaking as a resident more so than a

55:37.503 --> 55:41.205
developer. We don't have An end user, to clarify

55:41.705 --> 55:43.966
for everybody. We don't have a buyer right now. We don't have a builder.

55:44.946 --> 55:48.414
We want to make sure that we have this development agreement,

55:48.735 --> 55:53.536
this zoning in place, so that when we were to advertise it to something,

55:53.713 --> 55:56.410
we could somewhat control how we did it.

55:57.004 --> 56:00.023
And other applicants, you know, and I understand how it goes, but for others,

56:00.360 --> 56:03.347
they may own this land and they live in five states away, and they just

56:03.847 --> 56:07.450
send somebody to. develop it and give them, you know, hey,

56:08.066 --> 56:11.110
