01:15:22.924 --> 01:15:24.960
for any other development of that nature.

01:15:26.162 --> 01:15:28.615
So there is a proposed development agreement for your review.

01:15:29.753 --> 01:15:31.725
As was noted in the prior presentation,

01:15:33.120 --> 01:15:36.763
there's still some unknowns about what specifically the project will entail,

01:15:37.213 --> 01:15:40.568
and this agreement reflects that, uh, those unknowns. However,

01:15:40.585 --> 01:15:44.551
there are certain things that we know are going to be needed infrastructure-wise

01:15:45.051 --> 01:15:49.078
to support, uh, a data center use, which was ultimately what's being contemplated

01:15:49.578 --> 01:15:52.996
consistent with the neighborhood. Um, and so those—

01:15:53.655 --> 01:15:57.123
you can look through Article 5 of the agreement, and that governs the various types

01:15:57.623 --> 01:16:02.534
of infrastructure that would be implicated Uh, by the development

01:16:02.566 --> 01:16:05.392
that would be anticipated, uh, coming out of this agreement.

01:16:05.970 --> 01:16:10.000
So, uh, other than that, it follows kind of our standard form for

01:16:10.113 --> 01:16:13.517
other— all our other data center agreements that you've seen previously in

01:16:13.581 --> 01:16:17.178
relation. Um, uh, I will say that

01:16:17.678 --> 01:16:21.240
there are no, you know, tax incentives that are associated with this. Um,

01:16:21.914 --> 01:16:25.847
for some of the older agreements, there were. That's what was was necessary to

01:16:26.347 --> 01:16:30.033
get companies to come. Under the current landscape, that's just

01:16:30.533 --> 01:16:34.619
not a thing. And so there are no incentives that are associated

01:16:35.119 --> 01:16:38.708
with this. It's just a straight— these are the needs

01:16:39.208 --> 01:16:43.070
of the development that are going to take place. The uses

01:16:43.182 --> 01:16:47.224
would be data center with power generation as an accessory use

01:16:48.314 --> 01:16:53.414
to support the data centers. Additionally, it contemplates

01:16:53.914 --> 01:16:56.293
plates, infrastructure going in related to those uses, sewer, water, roads,

01:16:57.468 --> 01:17:01.443
natural gas infrastructure, and I think,

01:17:03.761 --> 01:17:06.963
yes, and, you know, and just power distribution.

01:17:07.794 --> 01:17:10.999
So with that, the rest of it is again

01:17:11.499 --> 01:17:15.250
just taken from our standard template for data center development agreements. I will say

01:17:15.395 --> 01:17:19.336
in relation to the comment in the prior Public hearing. I believe

01:17:19.385 --> 01:17:23.295
she's referencing Section 10.14 of the agreement regarding

01:17:23.327 --> 01:17:27.464
confidential information that relates to things like trade secrets, so you're not giving your competitors

01:17:27.964 --> 01:17:32.052
a business advantage, and other types similar

01:17:32.552 --> 01:17:35.012
types of confidential business information. It would still be subject to Grandma,

01:17:36.216 --> 01:17:39.903
and so there would be an independent person that would ultimately

01:17:40.016 --> 01:17:44.508
be the final decider as to whether or not something. Qualifies as confidential business

01:17:45.008 --> 01:17:48.506
information. It just puts an obligation on the city to, when we get

01:17:49.006 --> 01:17:51.926
a grandma request, to allow the, um,

01:17:52.842 --> 01:17:56.310
owner of the property to make— to, to see the grandma request and

01:17:56.810 --> 01:17:59.650
determine whether or not they want to make a confidential business information claim.

01:18:00.565 --> 01:18:04.113
And then, then the onus would be on them to defend that in any future

01:18:04.613 --> 01:18:08.609
proceedings, whether it would be, um, an appeal, uh, to the Chief

01:18:09.109 --> 01:18:12.848
Administrative Officer, an appeal to the Government Records Office, an appeal to the District Court,

01:18:12.912 --> 01:18:16.268
and so on. So that they would be bearing

01:18:16.300 --> 01:18:19.736
those costs if they're making that claim. So that's kind of just

01:18:20.236 --> 01:18:23.670
to clarify what that's about: is to avoid giving competitors an unfair advantage

01:18:24.329 --> 01:18:28.696
by manipulating open records laws to get secrets

01:18:28.824 --> 01:18:32.614
of the industry that other that their competitors may have

01:18:33.114 --> 01:18:35.170
and want to keep secret. So that's the nature of that clause.

01:18:37.837 --> 01:18:40.970
Okay. Questions for Marcus at this time?

01:18:42.577 --> 01:18:44.618
Okay. Commissioner Ricorsi.

01:18:45.357 --> 01:18:48.629
