01:20:20.412 --> 01:20:23.761
It actually taking that long, but it's to—

01:20:24.338 --> 01:20:28.008
it actually protects the city because those are the uses. It limits what

01:20:28.508 --> 01:20:31.725
they can do with the property notwithstanding the RTI zoning. Okay.

01:20:33.151 --> 01:20:36.837
I guess, is there any thought or benefit maybe to

01:20:36.997 --> 01:20:40.955
like a 10-year term with extensions for certain

01:20:41.227 --> 01:20:44.785
milestones or like, I don't know, do we ever do that? We haven't done that

01:20:45.285 --> 01:20:49.328
in the past with data centers, to be honest. We've put in sort

01:20:49.393 --> 01:20:53.572
of certain

01:20:55.040 --> 01:20:58.154
things that they need to— certain dates that they need to accomplish certain items now.

01:20:58.283 --> 01:21:01.348
And it's been— and that has varied development to development,

01:21:02.058 --> 01:21:05.059
you know. So with the QTS agreement,

01:21:05.140 --> 01:21:08.207
there was a certain milestone that they were supposed to reach within, I think,

